# 01 - Introduction to APIs

# Introduction to APIs

---

# Chapter Overview

Application Programming Interfaces (APIs) are the backbone of modern software communication.

Every time you:

- Open Instagram
- Transfer money using a banking app
- Book an Uber
- Order food from Swiggy or Zomato
- Watch Netflix
- Ask ChatGPT a question
- Sync files to Google Drive

your device is interacting with one or more APIs.

In today's enterprise environments, organizations rarely build standalone applications. Instead, applications communicate with dozens or even hundreds of internal and external services using APIs.

Understanding APIs is the first and most important step toward mastering API Security.

