# Real-World Analogy

Imagine a restaurant.

```
                 Restaurant Example

+----------------------------------------------+
|                  Customer                    |
+----------------------------------------------+
                |
                | Order Food
                v
+----------------------------------------------+
|                 Waiter (API)                 |
+----------------------------------------------+
                |
                | Sends Order
                v
+----------------------------------------------+
|                 Kitchen                      |
+----------------------------------------------+
                |
                | Prepares Food
                v
+----------------------------------------------+
|                 Waiter                       |
+----------------------------------------------+
                |
                | Delivers Food
                v
+----------------------------------------------+
|                Customer                      |
+----------------------------------------------+
```

In this analogy:

Customer = Client

Kitchen = Server

Waiter = API

Food = Data

The customer never enters the kitchen.

Similarly,

A client never directly accesses a server's internal logic or database.

Instead, all communication happens through APIs.

