# Components of an API

Every API generally consists of the following components.

## Client

The software requesting information.

Examples:

- Mobile app
- Browser
- Backend application
- IoT device
- Another API

---

## Server

The system providing the requested information.

---

## Endpoint

A specific URL where an API can be accessed.

Example:

```
https://api.company.com/users
```

---

## Request

Information sent by the client.

It may include:

- HTTP Method
- Headers
- Authentication
- Parameters
- Request Body

---

## Response

Information returned by the server.

Usually contains:

- Status Code
- Headers
- JSON Data
- Error Messages

---

## Data Format

Modern APIs commonly exchange data using:

- JSON
- XML
- Protocol Buffers
- YAML (less common)
- Plain Text

