# Why APIs Matter in Cybersecurity

APIs expose business functionality directly.

Examples include:

- Login
- Money Transfer
- Password Reset
- File Upload
- Payment Processing
- Customer Records
- Medical Records
- Employee Data

If these APIs are insecure, attackers may gain unauthorized access to critical systems and sensitive information.

---

# Common API Assets Worth Protecting

Organizations protect APIs because they often expose:

- Personally Identifiable Information (PII)
- Financial Records
- Health Records
- Authentication Tokens
- Customer Data
- Employee Data
- Business Secrets
- Source Code
- Intellectual Property
- Internal Services

APIs are often more valuable targets than traditional web pages because they provide direct access to business logic and data.

